# Next.js Conventions

## App Router only

This repo uses **Next.js 16 App Router**. Do not create a `pages/` directory — Pages Router is forbidden.

```
app/
├── layout.tsx           # Root layout (server component)
├── (docs)/              # Route group for docs website
│   ├── page.tsx
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── page.tsx
│   │   └── [slug]/page.tsx
│   ├── tokens/page.tsx
│   └── patterns/page.tsx
├── mcp/
│   └── route.ts         # MCP HTTP endpoint (Route Handler)
└── globals.css
```

## Root layout

Must include `AppRouterCacheProvider` from `@mui/material-nextjs/v15-appRouter` and the Neoflo theme:

```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
import { AppRouterCacheProvider } from '@mui/material-nextjs/v15-appRouter';
import { ThemeProvider } from '@mui/material/styles';
import CssBaseline from '@mui/material/CssBaseline';
import { neofloTheme } from '@/src/theme';

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        <AppRouterCacheProvider>
          <ThemeProvider theme={neofloTheme}>
            <CssBaseline />
            {children}
          </ThemeProvider>
        </AppRouterCacheProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## MCP endpoint as Route Handler

The MCP endpoint is a Next.js Route Handler:

```tsx
// app/mcp/route.ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { handleMcpRequest } from '@/src/mcp/server';

export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  // Optional: auth check
  const auth = req.headers.get('authorization');
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
    if (auth !== `Bearer ${process.env.MCP_TOKEN}`) {
      return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 });
    }
  }

  const body = await req.json();
  const result = await handleMcpRequest(body);
  return NextResponse.json(result);
}

// Allow GET for health checks
export async function GET() {
  return NextResponse.json({ status: 'ok', name: 'neoflo-atoms-mcp' });
}
```

## Server vs Client components

- **Default to server components** for docs pages (`app/(docs)/**`). Better performance.
- **Mark as `'use client'`** when:
  - Using `useState`, `useEffect`, or other hooks
  - Using interactive MUI components (most of them)
  - Using event handlers
  - Using browser APIs

```tsx
// ✅ Server component (default)
export default async function ComponentDocsPage({ params }: { params: { slug: string } }) {
  const data = await fetch(`/data/components/${params.slug}.json`);
  return <ComponentDocsView data={data} />;
}

// ✅ Client component (separate file)
'use client';
export function ComponentDocsView({ data }: Props) {
  const [tab, setTab] = useState(0);
  return <Tabs value={tab} onChange={(_, v) => setTab(v)}>...</Tabs>;
}
```

## Imports

Use the `@/` alias for absolute imports from the project root:

```tsx
// ✅ Right
import { Button } from '@/src/components/Button';
import { neofloTheme } from '@/src/theme';

// ❌ Avoid for deep imports
import { Button } from '../../../src/components/Button';
```

## Data fetching

Read `data/*.json` directly in server components — no API route needed:

```tsx
// app/(docs)/components/page.tsx
import componentsData from '@/data/components.json';

export default function ComponentsPage() {
  return (
    <div>
      {Object.values(componentsData).map(component => (
        <ComponentCard key={component.name} {...component} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Environment variables

- Public vars: prefix with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` (exposed to browser)
- Server-only vars: no prefix (only available in server components and route handlers)
- Required env vars must be documented in `.env.example`

```
# .env.local
MCP_TOKEN=<internal-shared-secret>
NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL=https://atoms.neoflo.ai
```

## Forbidden patterns

- ❌ No `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps` (Pages Router only)
- ❌ No `<Link>` from `next/link` for external URLs — use `<a>` with `target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"`
- ❌ No `next/image` for icons or SVGs — use the Phosphor set from `@/src/icons`, with the `Icon` suffix (`MagnifyingGlassIcon`)
- ❌ No mixing Pages and App routing
- ❌ No client-side data fetching for docs content — it's all static
